# Justified suppressions only — never add an entry here without the
# investigation that earned it. Re-verify each one whenever it starts
# blocking CI again (a base image bump can pick up a real fix).

# pip's own vendored internal dependency (pip/_vendor/msgpack), used only by
# pip's own HTTP cache — never imported or reachable by the running app
# (PATH always resolves python/gunicorn/celery to /opt/venv; the process
# never calls into pip at runtime). Confirmed present even in pip 26.2.1
# (the latest release as of 2026-09-16) via a real `trivy image` scan and a
# full filesystem search of the built image — not something this repo's
# Dockerfile can fix; only an upstream pip release that bumps its vendored
# copy can.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# Not an actual installed "setuptools 70.3.0" package: every real setuptools
# install in the built image (system and venv) is upgraded to 84.0.0 (see
# Dockerfile's `pip install --upgrade ... setuptools`) and a full filesystem
# search found no 70.3.0 directory/dist-info anywhere. This is very likely
# build-provenance metadata embedded in pip 26.2.1's own official wheel (the
# setuptools version pip's wheel was built with), which a metadata parser can
# mistake for an installed dependency. Confirmed via `trivy image` +
# filesystem search, 2026-09-16.
CVE-2025-47273
